Box86 patch 23 -- complete the Wine 11 Wayland listener ABI bridge.

Apply after patch 22 to Box86 commit 0579f8b9 plus the FINALPLAY15 complete
patch and patches 17--22.

AUDIT EVIDENCE

The RG353VS compositor is Sway 1.11 and a live WAYLAND_DEBUG registry capture
advertises zwlr_data_control_manager_v1.  The shipped Wine 11 winewayland.so
binds that protocol at version 1 and immediately installs a
zwlr_data_control_device_v1_listener.  It can later install the matching offer
and source listeners; its standard fallback also uses wl_data_source_listener.
Patch 17 knew none of those four proxy classes.  Its unknown-class path passed
the guest x86 callback table straight to native armhf libwayland-client and
even logged that it would crash.  An event on that proxy therefore had an
invalid ARM function pointer by construction.

The same audit found two callback declarations copied with too many arguments:
xdg_surface.configure is (data, object, serial), and wl_keyboard.key is
(data, object, serial, time, key, state).  Cdecl happened to let the guest
ignore the extra values, but the native ARM callback types were still wrong.

FIX

- bridge all four listener structs Wine 11 can install on its clipboard path;
- use the exact xdg_surface.configure and wl_keyboard.key signatures;
- load and call public wl_proxy_get_class() through Box86's native-library
  function table instead of dereferencing the private wl_proxy layout;
- serialize the fixed callback-slot registry during cold listener setup and
  reject slot exhaustion instead of passing a NULL table to libwayland;
- reject any still-unknown listener class with -1 rather than installing guest
  x86 addresses in a native ARM dispatch table.

Listener registration is a cold path.  This adds no render/audio logging and
makes no FPS claim.

